      "text": [
        "3226 - وَ قَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ :\n\"إِنَّ اَلنَّوَاوِيسَ شَكَتْ إِلَى اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ شِدَّةَ حَرِّهَا فَقَالَ لَهَا عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ \"أُسْكُتِي فَإِنَّ مَوَاضِعَ اَلْقُضَاةِ أَشَدُّ حَرّاً مِنْكِ\" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3226 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"Indeed, the graves complained to Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, about their intense heat. So Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, said to them: 'Be silent, for the places of judges are hotter than you.'\""
        ]
      }
